#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:6
msgid ""
"When troubleshooting Mattermost Calls, gathering the appropriate log "
"files for analysis is critical. The required logs include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:8
msgid "RTCD logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:10
msgid ""
"The location of the RTCD log file is determined by the settings in your "
"RTCD `config.toml` file. If you are running Calls using the integrated "
"RTCD, these logs are included within the standard Mattermost server logs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:12
msgid "Client logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:14
msgid ""
"You can retrieve basic client logs by running the `/call logs` slash "
"command to output the log for the most recent call. However, capturing "
"the JavaScript console logs is often more helpful. The method for "
"capturing these logs depends on your client:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:16
msgid ""
"**Desktop App:** While a call is in progress, navigate to **View > "
"Developer Tools > Developer Tools for Call Widget**. Next to the "
"**Filter** field, select **Verbose** from the log level drop-down menu to"
" view the debug output. To save the log, right-click within the console "
"and select **Save as...**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:18
msgid ""
"![Developer Tools for Call Widget](../../images/developer-tools-call-"
"widget.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:18
msgid "Developer Tools for Call Widget"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:20
msgid ""
"**Chrome browser:** Select the **More menu** (three vertical dots) next "
"to the address bar, then go to **More Tools > Developer Tools**. Select "
"the **Console** tab to view the output. Next to the **Filter** field, "
"select **Verbose** from the log level drop-down menu to view the debug "
"output. To save the log, right-click within the console and select **Save"
" as...**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:22
msgid "Client statistics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:24
msgid ""
"You can gather client call statistics by running the `/call stats` slash "
"command. While you can run this command during an active call, it is best"
" to run it immediately after a call concludes. This command provides "
"valuable information regarding the negotiated connection between the "
"client and RTCD, as well as statistics on media packets sent and lost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:26
msgid "Mattermost server logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:28
msgid ""
"The Mattermost server logs often contain entries related to the Calls "
"plugin. If you are using an external RTCD instance, these logs are "
"generally less critical than the RTCD and client logs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-logging.md:31
msgid ""
"Interpreting RTCD and client logs can be challenging, as the Interactive "
"Connectivity Establishment (ICE) negotiation during call setup often logs"
" expected and benign failure or error messages. We strongly recommend "
"providing the complete set of logs to Mattermost Support for analysis."
msgstr ""

